; Example zone fragment for DNS failover. Documentation range IPs (RFC 5737).
; Primary and secondary share one name; a health-checking DNS service (Route 53, etc.)
; answers with the primary until its health check fails, then switches to the secondary.
$ORIGIN example.com.
$TTL 60
orders  60  IN  A  192.0.2.10    ; PRIMARY   (health-checked)
orders  60  IN  A  198.51.100.10 ; SECONDARY (served only when primary is unhealthy)
; Low TTL = fast failover but more query load; 300s+ is typical for stable records.
